    "Same41 retained B3 closures and search cursors. Thirty-one cases contain161 verified failures on B3. Pilot exposed before timing; no holdout.",
    "Both arms check source, guards, all earlier failure layers and saved closures, cursor binding/schedule and every retained failed proof, then construct B4. Base propagates B3; feedback propagates B4. Zero new assumed probes.",
    "Only checked failed-probe consequences become units. Open-history claims provide no axioms. Native reconstruction expands every used consequence through strictly decreasing banks B4/B3/B2/B1/B0.",
    "Two opposite-order isolated repetitions per target and arm. Reconstruction, preparation, cursor validation, indexing and propagation are charged. Earlier acquisition, startup/loading and final audits are additional.",
    "Open B4 closures are reconstructed in a separate scan-based diagnostic with explicit timing/counters outside bounded discovery. Open or budget-limited outcomes never mean SAT.",
    "Fresh/native positive comparisons include warm checking, both cold readers and persistence, but exclude discovery, seed acquisition and unresolved fallback. Isolated archives can duplicate shared records; cumulative tables and production defaults remain unchanged.",
    "Old cursors still bind B3 and cannot be used to skip candidates on changed B4 banks. Fixed four-layer composition does not bound future contexts, proof expansion or retained history; no unrestricted-SAT conclusion."
